{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/pulls/7724","id":2116906614,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAacf885-LW52","html_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7724","diff_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7724.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7724.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/7724","number":7724,"state":"closed","locked":true,"title":"status: Fix status incompatibility introduced by #6919 and move non-regeneratable proto code into /testdata","user":{"login":"arjan-bal","id":46515553,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTE1NTUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46515553?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal","html_url":"https://github.com/arjan-bal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arjan-bal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/7679\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nhttps://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/6919 migrated usages of `github.com/golang/protobuf` to `google.golang.org/protobuf/proto` within `status` package. Prior to this, [status.Details()](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/blob/00b9e140ce71480ee7ecc6b85317021e0fe11fbb/internal/status/status.go#L150-L166) called `ptypes.UnmarshalAny` which called `proto.MessageV1(mt.New().Interface())` which called `protoimpl.X.ProtoMessageV1Of(m)` so the returned type always implemented `protoadapt.MessageV1` and was always the same type given to [status.WithDetails()](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/blob/00b9e140ce71480ee7ecc6b85317021e0fe11fbb/internal/status/status.go#L134-L148). After the change, `Status.Details()` used `anpb.Any.UnmarshallNew()` which returns the vanilla type used while creating the `anypb.Any` which is only guaranteed to implement the `MessageV2` API. \r\n\r\n## Effect\r\nUsers of code generated from `protoc-gen-go` < v1.4 (launched in 2020) would get a wrapped MessageV2 when calling `Status.Details()` even though they would have provided a type that only implemented `MessageV1` to `Status.WithDetails()`.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\nThis PR brings back the call to `protoimpl.X.ProtoMessageV1Of(m)` by calling `protoadapt.MessageV1Of` before returning the Detail messages. A test is also added to catch regressions. Since the test uses generated code from `protoc-gen-go` v1.3, a dependency on `github.com/golang/protobuf` is re-introduced in `go.mod`.\r\n\r\n## Additional Changes\r\nThis PR also moves the generated code that is used for testing and must not be re-generated from the `reflections/test` module into a common directory under the parent `grpc` module.\r\n\r\nRELEASE NOTES:\r\n* status: Fix regression caused by #6919 in status.Details() causing it to return a wrapped type when getting proto messages generated with protoc-gen-go < v1.4.","created_at":"2024-10-10T07:38:15Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T02:03:18Z","closed_at":"2024-10-22T17:46:16Z","merged_at":"2024-10-22T17:46:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"4bb0170ac65f2726d593eb7364a807b171fa1d63","assignees":[{"login":"easwars","id":1638487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg0ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1638487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars","html_url":"https://github.com/easwars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/following{/oth